# Documentation stays current

Never finish a backend change with stale documentation. Update matching pages in the same change. Do not defer docs to a later task.

## Where docs live

- Product, screens, API, permissions, data model, onboarding, limitations: `payroll-frontend/docs/`
- User-facing workflow or copy changes: also `payroll-frontend/src/docs/content/`
- Startup, package location, request flow: this repository `README.md` and `docs/`

## When to update

Update whenever an endpoint, permission, entity, schema, scheduler, integration, runtime requirement, or operator procedure changes.

Skip only no-behavior edits (formatting, comments, unused-code cleanup). If you skip, say so in the reply.

Treat current code as current behavior and label gaps explicitly. Never add credentials, tokens, personal data, salary data, or production endpoints.

After editing the frontend portal, run `npm run docs:check` in `payroll-frontend`.
